lour, heated in cream or milk, and seasoned with ground nutmeg. Béchamel is one of the mother sauces of French cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bechamel"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9chamel"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku",[["Doria (food)","dish/doria-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Béchamel sauce","ingredient/bechamel-sauce"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Pilaf","ingredient/pilaf"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8a/2021_Sos_beszamelowy.jpg/500px-2021_Sos_beszamelowy.jpg","w":500,"h":352,"by":"Jacek Halicki","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2021_Sos_beszamelowy.jpg"}},"ingredient/whitefish":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/whitefish","n":"Whitefish","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 5 cuisines","intro":[["Whitefish or white fish is a fisheries term for several species of demersal fish with fins, particularly Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua), whiting (Merluccius bilinearis), haddock (Melanogrammus aeglefinus), hake (Urophycis), and pollock (Pollachius), among others."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-whitefish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitefish_(fisheries_term)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":5,"groups":[["Alaska Native foodways","cuisine/alaska-native-foodways",[["Akutaq","dish/akutaq"]]],["Athabascan foodways","cuisine/athabascan-foodways",[["Akutaq","dish/akutaq"]]],["Iñupiaq foodways","cuisine/inupiaq-foodways",[["Akutaq","dish/akutaq"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Gefilte fish","dish/gefilte-fish"]]],["Yup'ik cuisine","cuisine/yup-ik-cuisine",[["Akutaq","dish/akutaq"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Carrot","ingredient/c